---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";

// Boilerplate tied to the same legal entity as the other sites this operator
// runs, which is why it is noindex and excluded from the sitemap. The
// registered office is hardcoded here on purpose: it is the REGISTERED address,
// not the trading address in business.ts, and editing business.ts must never
// silently change it.
const REGISTERED_OFFICE = "Dorset House, 5 Church Street, Wimborne, Dorset, BH21 1JH";
const lastUpdated = "23 August 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Roof Repairs Croydon"
  description="How Roof Repairs Croydon collects, uses and stores the personal data you send through this website."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="bg-ink text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        <a href="/" class="text-white hover:text-brand-light transition-colors">Privacy Policy</a>
      </h1>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-light">How we handle your information</h2>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-base font-semibold text-steel-light">Last updated {lastUpdated}</h3>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 prose prose-stone prose-a:text-brand-dark">
    <h2>Who controls your data</h2>
    <p>
      This website trades as {business.name}. It is owned and operated by {business.siteOperator.name},
      company number {business.siteOperator.companyNumber}, registered office {REGISTERED_OFFICE}.
      {business.siteOperator.name} is the data controller for information submitted through this
      site.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you ask for a survey or a quote, your enquiry is passed to the roofing company that
      carries out the work. That company acts as a separate data controller for the purposes of
      quoting for and carrying out roofing work, and you will be told who they are before any
      agreement is made.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Through the enquiry forms on this site we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name;</li>
      <li>your email address;</li>
      <li>your telephone number;</li>
      <li>the service you have selected, and any detail you add;</li>
      <li>the page the enquiry was sent from.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not use analytics cookies, advertising cookies or third-party trackers on this site,
      and there is no cookie banner because there is nothing to consent to.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      Solely to respond to your enquiry: to contact you, arrange a survey, prepare a quote and, if
      you go ahead, carry out and guarantee the work. We do not sell your data, we do not share it
      with unrelated third parties, and we do not add you to a marketing list on the strength of an
      enquiry.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      For responding to an enquiry, our legal basis is legitimate interests - you have asked us to
      get in touch and it is reasonable for us to do so. Once you engage us for work, the basis
      becomes performance of a contract. Where we keep records to support a guarantee, the basis is
      again legitimate interests together with our legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>Who your information is shared with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, which processes the form submission and delivers it to us by
        email. Their privacy terms are published at web3forms.com.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The roofing contractor</strong> who surveys, quotes for and carries out the work.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our email provider</strong>, which stores the message in the ordinary course.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not transfer your data outside the UK or the EEA for any other purpose.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not become work are deleted within 12 months. Where work is carried out, we
      keep the record for the duration of the workmanship guarantee plus a further period to cover
      any claim arising from it, because a guarantee cannot be honoured without a record of the job.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask what personal data we hold about you and get a copy of it;</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
      <li>ask us to erase your data where we have no continuing reason to keep it;</li>
      <li>restrict or object to our processing;</li>
      <li>ask for your data in a portable format;</li>
      <li>withdraw consent where consent was the basis for processing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these, email
      {" "}<a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>. We will respond within one
      month.
    </p>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, please tell us first so we have the
      chance to put it right. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's
      Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>,
      or on 0303 123 1113.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      This site is served over HTTPS and form submissions are encrypted in transit. Access to
      enquiry data is limited to the people who need it to respond to you and to carry out the
      work.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {business.siteOperator.name}, {REGISTERED_OFFICE}.<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a><br />
      Telephone: <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
